Use memchr to find each newline in the buffer. The line length includes the
newline character itself. If the last chunk has no newline, it runs to the end
of the buffer.

When checking a line, use strnstr(line_start, target, line_len) for each entry
in content_targets. strnstr is bounded, so it will not read past the line.

When you remove a line, memmove everything after it backward, subtract
line_len from new_total, and do not advance your position pointer. The next
line is now at the current position.
